  "result": "Fixed. The `--help` output was showing the names within each option in the wrong order: `--verbose, -v` instead of `-v, --verbose`.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` sorts an option's names by prefix length so that `-v` comes before `--verbose`. The sort had `reverse=True`, so long names came first. I removed that flag. Python's sort is stable, so names with the same prefix length keep the order they were declared in.\n\nBefore and after:\n```\n--verbose, -v  verbose     \u2192     -v, --verbose  verbose\n```\n\nThe order of the options themselves (declaration order, with `--help` last) was already correct and hasn't changed.\n\n**Tests:** Nothing in the suite checked this, so I added `test_help_short_options_listed_first` to `tests/test_formatting.py`. It covers short and long names declared in either order, `--foo/--no-foo` flags, and slash-prefixed options. The full suite passes: 1910 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed. I didn't run the new test against the old code to see it fail.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
